2.1.2 In-Vehicle Information Systems versus Advanced Driver Assistance Systems

ADAS vs In-car driver support systems can be categorized based on their goals towards comfort and

IVIS

safety. Such systems distinguish between driver information systems (In-vehicle Informa-

tion Systems, IVIS) and driver assistance systems (Advanced Driver Assistance Systems,

ADAS). Driver information systems are designed to inform and entertain the user while driv-

ing. Examples are air condition control, radio control and multimedia systems. Driver as-

sistance systems explicitly support drivers in their driving task. Examples are heading or

