Since secondary tasks are not as important as primary tasks, immediate accessibility does not play such a fundamental role. Direct access should be granted, but access to the devices must not be as direct as for primary controls. Tertiary devices do not have a direct relationship to the driving task itself or to safety issues. Immediate and direct access is not necessary. Multi-functional controllers can be incorporated because no one to one mapping is required.

